    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under real traffic. It is designed to catch the failure modes that single-node testing misses: silent rank divergence, partial-failure states, accounting drift, and timing artifacts from measurement infrastructure itself.\n\n**How to use this checklist:** Each item is a gate. A system is not \"validated\" until every applicable item passes with recorded evidence. Items marked **[CRITICAL]** invalidate all downstream results if they fail.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every process in the cluster is executing the same logical system.\n\n### 1.1 Model and Weight Identity\n- [ ] **[CRITICAL]** Record the model artifact hash (weight file checksums, not just the path or version tag). All ranks must load from the same verified artifact. A path alone is insufficient \u2014 a stale cache or partially-written checkpoint can pass a path check.\n- [ ] **[CRITICAL]** Verify tokenizer identity across all ranks: vocabulary hash, special-token map, and any post-tokenization normalization. Tokenizer drift between ranks produces silently corrupted sequences in pipeline-parallel setups.\n- [ ] Confirm quantization/serving precision (fp16, bf16, int8, etc.) is identical on all ranks and matches the intended deployment spec. Mixed precision across ranks is a common misconfiguration in heterogeneous clusters.\n- [ ] Verify any LoRA/adapters, system prompts, or default sampling parameters are pinned and hashed, not referenced by mutable name.\n\n### 1.2 Code and Runtime Identity\n- [ ] **[CRITICAL]** Record the exact serving-framework version, commit hash if built from source, and any local patches. \"Latest\" is not a version.\n- [ ] Verify all ranks run the same binary/container image (image",
